Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:32:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 099/154] fix(hints): give every hover hint one style, and draw
 the sidebar's above the card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The floating address bar was not styling its hints differently, it had none:
those buttons carried a plain title attribute, so the platform drew a native
tooltip. They use the shared bubble now.

A sidebar hint was clipped at the sidebar's edge because each WebContents
renders into a surface hard-clipped to its own bounds, so no stacking rule
inside the page can reach past it. The hint moves to a full-window overlay
widget, the same mechanism the command bar and the peek already use to draw over
content. Corner-anchored hints stay in the page, since nothing clips them.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index b1e1fe9b119c2..070442183a45d 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -3593,6 +3593,8 @@ static_library("ui") {
       "atrium/atrium_command_dispatcher_delegate.mm",
       "atrium/atrium_extension_pill_widget.h",
